<report>
<line><title>McNemar and exact (Liddell) test for a paired fourfold table</title></line>
<line></line>
<line><b>Input table:</b></line>
<table>
<tr><td><in>tab_a1</in></td><td><in>tab_b1</in></td></tr>
<tr><td><in>tab_a2</in></td><td><in>tab_b2</in></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>Uncorrected Chi&#xb2; = <in>chi</in> (1 DF)  <ci><in>chi_p</in></ci></line>
<line>Yates' continuity corrected Chi&#xb2; = <in>yates_chi</in> (1 DF)  <ci><in>yates_chi_p</in></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line><b>After Liddell (1983):</b></line>
<line>Point estimate of relative risk (R') = <in>risk</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Exact <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>F = <in>f</in></line>
<line><ci>Two sided <in>tail_2</in></ci><block name="r_prime"></line>
<line></line>
<line>R' is significantly different from unity</block></line>
<line></line>
<line></line>
</report>
